    {
      "question": "e-21657",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "8d29b76e739461935f484d7f401650deb0f6d48790f4e5d27ceed92fd043242b",
      "new_sha256": "dd8c6f3ab41207fa1f8485bb4b56900337be4b26b2dbe879881e86f4109d9eec",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21657",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the system of linear differential equations below.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(t)=-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}(t)=9x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_{1,2} = \\pm3\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are $\\mathbf{v}_{1,2} = [\\pm \\text{i}, 3]^T,$ respectively. Given that the general solution of the system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/assets/6feea8db62000e44334251a96c39bd8d0d8d7b1ec9a61380f3a5b4b613ea6c80.png)\nsketch the phase portrait of the system of differential equations given above.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/example-21657.json",
          "file_sha256": "4b7c7262421ecc8b697bbc70c7b24086df869e1eef0f58e54d33b896110cd67b"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2398,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2399
    },
    {
      "question": "e-21657",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "fa0dbe96424541467bd8dec522fe8b3b46521507bc2abdc793cf8775163e5cd3",
      "new_sha256": "558544bfdaba3ee8a0df33475bbfbc367db6cc0139de7721b981b0d5ca431c21",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21657",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We are given that the general solution of the system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/assets/bceb494a6baeca8695157b4fd285b2880a242367747c0d72a0f573612ef87652.png)\n\nFor example, when $c_1=1$ and $c_2=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3t) \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-0.71$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2.12$ | $0$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/assets/3c2ea4467854f749e07f5ae3922273a2ebd441da4fb9df834ce0676157e856a2.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\sin(3t)| \\leq 1$ and $|\\cos(3t)| \\leq 1.$ Thus, the obtained curve is bounded. So, we have an ellipse that is traversed counterclockwise.\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/assets/df8e7ae5f7ff7281cbdbf5849dc94faf59d2421621dc5009b21eeb947485d153.png)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/example-21657.json",
          "file_sha256": "4b7c7262421ecc8b697bbc70c7b24086df869e1eef0f58e54d33b896110cd67b"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2398,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069757/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2399
    },
    {
